        <mxCell id="e43" value="caused" style="edgeStyle=entityRelationEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;startArrow=ERone;startFill=0;endArrow=ERmany;endFill=0;strokeColor=#4a5468;fontColor=#4a5468;exitX=0.5;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=1;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="entity" target="trip_leg"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n4" value="started_at and ended_at are when the work was done and zone is where, so it is shown as it was worked; seconds is worked out from them by the server, and worked_on is the day it started there. An entry recorded before it kept its times has its length alone.

worked_by is who worked the hour, and crew says whether it bills at one person&apos;s rate or the team&apos;s; created_by is who entered it, which is how the row is explained later.

client_uuid is made on the phone: the offline queue retries, and without it a retry that timed out enters the hour twice.

Work done by the whole crew is one row with crew = team, so its billable quantity is recorded, not worked out. Anyone who carries on alone afterwards gets a row of their own at crew = one.

A team row has no worked_by. created_by is whoever ran the timer, and user.role_id is what decides pay.

The team is every active person with a role; that number is the head count a team row is priced and paid at.

trip_leg.service_id is what a billed leg bills as, so nothing has to assume that only one service is charged per mile." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontColor=#7b8698;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="830" width="1180" height="350" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
